 dedicated exclusive fcntl.flock'","'fcntl matches the existing HLC-sidecar precedent in-tree' — fcntl is a POSIX-only stdlib module absent on Windows"],"finding":"The mechanism relies on fcntl.flock, which does not exist on Windows (the fcntl module is POSIX-only). Windows is a supported platform in the matrix. Although the plan cites the HLC-sidecar fcntl precedent, adding a new fcntl import/lock site on the create path can raise ImportError/AttributeError at import or lock time; the plan's graceful-degradation clause covers runtime probe failures, not an fcntl unavailability at import.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f36f303074942c1fa","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Design — Concurrency: 'a dedicated exclusive fcntl.flock on the sidecar recent-creates.lock' and Portability: 'fcntl matches the existing HLC-sidecar precedent in-tree'","norm_id":"n4d4fd8f61f4bba16","priority":0.0,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Windows platform, flag on: importing/using fcntl in recent_creates.py fails (module missing), and if not guarded the create can crash or the probe throws before the degrade branch is reached."],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"Wrap the fcntl import and lock acquisition so that on ImportError/OSError the probe degrades to no-warning (matching the existing degrade contract), and note this in the design.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.3125,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"insufficient","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","